    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Communication strategies in Dutch",
     "texto": [
      "To manage a real conversation when the other person speaks too fast or in a noisy setting, essential polite phrases are used: «Kunt u dat herhalen?» (Can you repeat that?), «Ik versta u niet goed» (I don't hear or understand you well) and «Langzamer, alstublieft» (more slowly, please). To check the time: «half vier» is half past three (15:30), not half past four."
     ],
